Ritemark Launch Check: the Node line only where a runtime needs Node.js
The Welcome page's launch check said "Ritemark needs Node." on any
machine without `node` on PATH, on macOS and Windows alike, whatever the
Runtime preference. The agent runtimes Ritemark bundles need no system
Node.js: Claude Code 2.1.281 is a self-contained binary the Agent SDK
spawns directly, and the Codex 0.154.0 app server is a native Rust
binary (checked 2026-09-26 against the shipped packages, PR #359).
Node.js matters only when the user's own Claude or Codex came from npm.

The extension already decides when that is: Windows with Runtime
preference "Use system install" (setup.ts systemRuntimeToolsRequired).
ritemark.getHealthStatus now sends it as nodeRequired, and the Node line
renders only when it is true. An extension older than the field sends
nothing, so the line stays hidden, which is the right answer for the
bundled runtimes.

The Git line is unchanged: Source Control needs Git. No install link
comes back (016, Microsoft Store policy 10.1.5).

Applies after 016, whose comment and launch-check lines it builds on;
001 owns the launch-check list itself.
---
diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/browser/gettingStarted.ts b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/browser/gettingStarted.ts
index 30a2920dcc4..57ab9550776 100644
--- a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/browser/gettingStarted.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/browser/gettingStarted.ts
@@ -1099,6 +1099,7 @@ export class GettingStartedPage extends EditorPane {
 					claudeAvailable: boolean;
 					claudeAuthenticated: boolean;
 					nodeInstalled: boolean;
+					nodeRequired?: boolean;
 					nodeVersion: string | null;
 					gitInstalled: boolean;
 					gitVersion: string | null;
@@ -1112,6 +1113,7 @@ export class GettingStartedPage extends EditorPane {
 						claudeAvailable: boolean;
 						claudeAuthenticated: boolean;
 						nodeInstalled: boolean;
+						nodeRequired?: boolean;
 						nodeVersion: string | null;
 						gitInstalled: boolean;
 						gitVersion: string | null;
@@ -1198,12 +1200,19 @@ export class GettingStartedPage extends EditorPane {
 			// Same rule as the Git check above. Not flagged by the report, but
 			// the identical construct — fixing only what was reported would
 			// leave the same exposure for the next certification round.
-			container.appendChild(renderLaunchCheckItem(
-				status.nodeInstalled
-					? localize('ritemark.nodeReady', "Ritemark found Node.")
-					: localize('ritemark.nodeMissing', "Ritemark needs Node."),
-				status.nodeInstalled
-			));
+			//
+			// The bundled agent runtimes do not need Node.js, so this line
+			// appears only when the extension reports that one of the user's
+			// own runtimes does (nodeRequired). An extension older than that
+			// field sends nothing, and the line stays hidden.
+			if (status.nodeRequired) {
+				container.appendChild(renderLaunchCheckItem(
+					status.nodeInstalled
+						? localize('ritemark.nodeReady', "Ritemark found Node.")
+						: localize('ritemark.nodeMissing', "Ritemark needs Node."),
+					status.nodeInstalled
+				));
+			}
 		} catch {
 			container.textContent = '';
 			container.appendChild(renderLaunchCheckItem(localize('ritemark.healthError', "Could not check status."), false));
